From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] lumaShare: a screen tile shows exactly its screen

Each screen tile cloned global.window_group and was meant to offset and
scale it onto its monitor, but the clone was allocated at the stage's
origin, so the offset never applied: every tile showed the whole
multi-monitor stage squashed into it. The tile's name and resolution came
from listDisplays() by position, but that list is sorted for naming
(built-in first) while tiles follow the layout's monitor order, so a tile
could carry another monitor's name, its connector -- the screen actually
shared -- and a size that was a layout size, not the display's.

A screen tile now holds that monitor at 1:1, scaled into the tile at the
monitor's own aspect and clipped to it: the background, the windows on
that monitor and the Shell's chrome there (shelf, bar), each a clone bound
to where its source is, less the monitor's origin. Only what is on the
monitor is cloned, so a tile repaints only that monitor; dialogs (the
picker itself), the lock screen, the overview and anything held back from
captures are never cloned. The set is resynced on restack and at most once
a second for windows moving between monitors. A tile takes the display
whose layout index is its monitor's, and shows that display's current
mode in pixels (listDisplays() now returns it).

diff --git a/js/ui/lumaCast.js b/js/ui/lumaCast.js
index f7de746..fc6233b 100644
--- a/js/ui/lumaCast.js
+++ b/js/ui/lumaCast.js
@@ -179,13 +179,16 @@ export async function listDisplays() {
                 inLayout.add(connector);
         }
         const displays = monitors
-            .map(([[connector], , props]) => {
+            .map(([[connector], modes, props]) => {
                 const p = unpackDict(props);
+                // The current mode: the display's resolution in pixels.
+                const current = modes.find(mode => unpackDict(mode[6])['is-current']);
                 return {
                     connector,
                     builtin: Boolean(p['is-builtin']),
                     name: p['is-builtin'] ? _('Built-in display') : (p['display-name'] || connector),
                     index: manager.get_monitor_for_connector(connector),
+                    mode: current ? [current[1], current[2]] : null,
                 };
             })
             .filter(d => inLayout.has(d.connector) && d.index >= 0)
diff --git a/js/ui/lumaShare.js b/js/ui/lumaShare.js
index 22f02ac..8d4d664 100644
--- a/js/ui/lumaShare.js
+++ b/js/ui/lumaShare.js
@@ -313,10 +313,19 @@ const PreviewTile = GObject.registerClass({
     }
